Q: How to keep key case sensitive in HTTP request header using Golang? A: <p>The <a href="http://godoc.org/net/http#Header" rel="noreferrer">http.Header</a> <a href="http://godoc.org/net/http#Header.Add" rel="noreferrer">Add</a> and <a href="http://godoc.org/net/http#Header.Set" rel="noreferrer">Set</a> methods canonicalize the header name when adding values to the header map. You can sneak around the canonicalization by adding values using map operations:</p>

<pre><code>request.Header["MyKey"] = []string{"MyValue"}
request.Header["MYKEY2"] = []string{"MyNewValue"}
request.Header["DONT-CHANGE-ME"] = []string{"No"}
</code></pre>

<p>As long as you use canonical names for headers known to the transport, this should work.</p>
